  "worked_solution": "We're given that $y=\\frac{1}{A-x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=3.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=3$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{A-x} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{A-0} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{A} \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
